NOTE: This is for demo purposes only. This demo uses a few .h files and .cpp files before extra commits were made to them. Feel free to integrate whatever for the actual main branch though.


How to build:

cd ~/Mission-Level-Route-Planner/ros2_ws
source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
colcon build --packages-select mission_level_route_planner
source install/setup.bash


How to test:

colcon test --packages-select mission_level_route_planner --event-handlers console_direct+
colcon test-result --verbose

You should see 3 test programs pass: test_dijkstra (14 tests), test_altitude_limits (9) and test_safety_margin (16), 39 in total.





EXTRA EXTRA EXTRA EXTRA EXTRA EXTRA

To run only the safety margin tests, run the test program directly (the path is usually right):

./build/mission_level_route_planner/test_safety_margin

(Add --gtest_filter=SafetyMargin.PathKeeps* to run just one test.)

To see the margin work:

optionally add this line to src/planner_demo.cpp, right before the Context ctx(...) line:

grid->set_safety_margin(1.5);

Rebuild and run it with ros2 run mission_level_route_planner planner_demo.
